        {
          "atom": "banana_ester_notes",
          "why": "Estolides are fatty acid oligomers, NOT isoamyl acetate. Isoamyl acetate is a simple ester. The atom incorrectly claims estolide_compounds are primarily isoamyl acetate - conflating two unrelated chemical classes.",
          "price": 49,
          "url": "https://github.com/sancovp/dark-factory-live/issues/53"
        },
        {
          "atom": "crust",
          "why": "Claims crust texture depends on hydration and baking method. Wrong: crust texture is primarily driven by steam and oven temperature, not dough hydration. Hydration affects crumb, not crust texture.",
          "price": 2,
          "url": "https://github.com/sancovp/dark-factory-live/issues/54"
        },
        {
          "atom": "dough_temperature",
          "why": "Claims 75-80F ensures predictable timing regardless of room conditions. This overpromises: 75F is borderline cool for sourdough (optimal is 78-82F); room temperature still meaningfully affects outcomes. A user at 65F room with 75F dough will get slow fermentation despite targeting the stated range.",
          "price": 12,
          "url": "https://github.com/sancovp/dark-factory-live/issues/55"
        },
        {
          "atom": "baking_temperature",
          "why": "Range of 450-500F is so wide as to mislead. Dutch oven sourdough typically bakes at 475-500F. A user picking 450F from this range will likely get a gummy, underbaked crumb - the crust wont set properly at that temperature for standard sourdough hydration levels.",
          "price": 4,
          "url": "https://github.com/sancovp/dark-factory-live/issues/56"
        }
      ]
    },
